Description: sticky note application for the desktop (XNote, GTK 4 fork)
 XNote is a sticky note application that strives to be simple, fault-tolerant
 and customizable. XNote consists of independent pad windows, each being a text
 box in which notes can be written.
 .
 This is the XNote fork (renamed from xpad), ported from GTK 3 to GTK 4 +
 libadwaita. Existing notes are automatically migrated from ~/.config/xpad on
 first launch. The tray icon is provided via the freedesktop StatusNotifierItem
 protocol (visible through the GNOME AppIndicator extension). XNote is native
 Wayland and does not directly link against X11 libraries.
